  message: "Fixed in PR #2347. Close condition, part 1 (the factory refuses or repairs, with a test): on dev 49bc5c6e4 ir._canonical_external_id('python', '', 'x') returns python:<external>:0-0:x:external_symbol (ADR-0036 Ruling 3's sentinel) and ir._canonical_external_id('python', 'm', '') raises ValueError ('boundary id for python:'m' has an empty name slot'); test packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_boundary_id_empty_slots.py. The producers that passed an empty slot (js_ts, go, js_module empty import specifiers) are fixed at their source (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_empty_import_specifier.py). Part 2 (survey counts 0): a fixture of empty specifiers in 12 languages gives 28 nodes, 16 edges, 0 ids with an empty slot, id_format 0 on dev 49bc5c6e4 (the build measured 4 id_format violations on it before the fix); eight repositories run on dev 49bc5c6e4 (openzeppelin, koel, workadventure front, hocuspocus, metabase bin, spring-petclinic, alertmanager, knex) have 0 empty-slot ids among node ids and edge endpoints and id_format 0; the branch run over 42 repositories had id_format 0. NOT asserted: make_symbol_id and make_file_id still accept an empty path or name for an emitted symbol; that needs a ruling and is filed as WI-hodin-kizis-nugir-simuv-ritat-vihuz-vatof-jiris (point 2). Outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/closure/ (fixtures*.txt, trees_summary.txt, pair_check_dev.txt)."  # 362e
